PavVault Privacy Policy

Effective date: July 2026

1. Introduction

PavVault respects your privacy and is designed to help users organize and manage their product warranties, receipts and important documents.

This Privacy Policy explains how information is stored and handled when using the application.



2. Information Stored

PavVault may store information entered by the user, including:

• Product names
• Store or seller names
• Purchase dates
• Warranty expiration dates
• Product categories
• Product prices
• Receipt images
• Warranty documents


3. Data Storage

Your information is stored locally on your device.

PavVault does not upload, sell, rent or share your personal information with third parties.

Future features such as cloud backup may require changes to this Privacy Policy and will only operate after user consent.



4. Receipt Images and Documents

Documents added to PavVault remain private and are stored for the purpose of helping users manage their own warranties.

Users are responsible for ensuring they have legal rights to store the documents they add.



5. Notifications

Warranty reminders are generated locally on your device to inform you about upcoming warranty expirations.



6. Data Security

PavVault provides optional PIN protection to help prevent unauthorized access.

Users are responsible for protecting access to their device and keeping their PIN secure.



7. Data Loss

Users are responsible for maintaining backups of their own information.

PavVault is not responsible for loss of data caused by device damage, device replacement, accidental deletion, operating system issues, or other circumstances outside reasonable control.



8. Third Party Services

Currently, PavVault does not share user data with third-party services.

If future features require third-party services, this Privacy Policy will be updated accordingly.



9. Your Rights

Users may delete their stored information at any time by removing data from the application or uninstalling the application.



10. Contact

For questions regarding privacy, please contact:

